{"nodes": [{"id": "lib_orchestrator_deployformation", "label": "deployFormation Pipeline", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "lib/orchestrator.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Clone is bounded at LC_CLONE_CONCURRENCY (8) and configure at LC_CONFIGURE_CONCURRENCY (4) because a linked clone is a short disk op while in-guest configuration occupies the VM for tens of minutes. DHCP leases are created strictly sequentially since pfSense does read-modify-write on config.xml. If applyDhcpChanges fails every surviving VM is failed, because without applied reservations VMs would take arbitrary pool addresses and Guacamole would point at the wrong host."}, {"id": "lib_orchestrator_loadselection", "label": "loadSelection", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "lib/orchestrator.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns null for formations created before migration 004 that have no os_id \u2014 they stay deployable, just without in-guest configuration."}, {"id": "db_formations_table", "label": "formations Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "lib/orchestrator.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds the status state machine (draft, deploying, deployed, failed, deleting, cleanup_failed) and the encrypted vm_password; deleting the row cascades to jobs and formation_vms."}, {"id": "db_formation_vms_table", "label": "formation_vms Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "lib/orchestrator.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-VM record of truth: vmid, ip, mac_address, dhcp_lease_id, guac_username, guac_connection_id \u2014 teardown reads exactly these fields to know what external resources exist."}], "edges": [{"source": "